    "introduction": "Hiscox provides specialist insurance and reinsurance to individuals, businesses and other insurers. Its activities include small-business cover, insurance for valuable personal assets and larger commercial risks handled through the London market. Reinsurance allows it to take on portions of risks originally written by other insurers. Income comes from underwriting and investing funds held against future claims. Its model depends on understanding complex risks, setting appropriate premiums and controlling aggregate exposure. Claims from catastrophes or liability events can emerge unevenly over time. Distribution through brokers, partners and direct channels gives it several routes to customers, while underwriting discipline is central to profitability.",
